  "ingredients": [
    "3 cups all-purpose flour",
    "2 cups white sugar",
    "1 teaspoon baking soda",
    "1 teaspoon salt",
    "2 cups mashed bananas",
    "1.5 cups canola oil",
    "1 cup chopped black walnuts",
    "1 (8 ounce) can crushed pineapple, drained",
    "3 large eggs",
    "1 pound confectioners' sugar",
    "1 (8 ounce) package cream cheese, softened",
    "0.25 pound butter, softened",
    "1 teaspoon vanilla extract"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Grease and flour two 9-inch cake pans.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/OIIOoBBnP9VHROiEzlEMNThc3sg=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/15750-humminhbird-cake-ddmfs-Step1-1256-dab95b86f9224faea3498c8ce87a2b2c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/15750/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "To make the cake: Sift flour, sugar, baking soda, and salt together in a large bowl. Combine bananas, oil, walnuts, pineapple, and eggs in another large bowl; mix well.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/SnNs84gGu_gHQ54Ry041AeBp-6c=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/15750-humminhbird-cake-ddmfs-Step2-1258-4beef466305d4dfa96f5bade4be3201e.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/15750/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir flour mixture into banana mixture until combined. Pour batter into the prepared pans.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/7-MsV5wB-PsrusMkh_1pYB10xH8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/15750-humminhbird-cake-ddmfs-Step3-1260-021434542fe444bc89f733934895f2b4.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/15750/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until a toothpick inserted into the center of each pan comes out clean, about 1 hour. Allow cakes to cool on wire racks.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/2A4EJoaB7nZgEyr2uke6IZbQOeE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/15750-humminhbird-cake-ddmfs-Step4-1275-b8519815d6224395a8795eda21c3229c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/15750/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, make the frosting: Beat confectioners' sugar, cream cheese, butter, and vanilla together in a medium bowl until smooth.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Place one cooled cake on a serving plate or cake stand. Spread some of the cream cheese frosting on top of cake; place second cake on top and spread remaining frosting evenly over the surface and sides of the cake.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/ml7ID1kwKLdzaQ8iLt-01w7jFyU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/15750-hummingbird-cake-Kim-Shupe-horizontal-4x3-4bdcb723dba1486aacd1e704a274af3f.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/15750/step_06.webp"
    }
  ],
